From 5dbe2228d7586a36e4f1adc394f4414357fb5318 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tbrasselle <tbrasselle@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 11:28:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(motion): refuse a Linear comp lead whose dive rides the
 ring line

#3891: a Linear lead-in starts on the ring's own offset line, so the
Plunge's dive at its start - and the Arc entry's chord, whose XY
footprint lands on that same point - post under G40 one nominal radius
off the finished wall. A register over the nominal radius, or a
positive wear value over the stock, cuts the wall there before
G41/G42 engages. The mirrored Linear lead-out repeats the defect at
the cancel's end, past G40.

contour_comp::door refuses the Linear shape for both ends, by name,
and the #3888 note that cleared the dive is corrected: the door's
lead-length law holds the dive clear only for the Perpendicular
shape, whose start stands its length further into the air. That
clearance - one full radius beyond the ring line, re-checked on the
actual moves by push_span - is the maximum register difference the
door vouches for. The pins read the posted G-code: under an
oversized register (5.0 mm on the D6 tool) and a positive wear value
(1.0 mm), no stand under G40 touches the finished wall, and the
closest stand is the dive point itself, the radius plus the lead.

The comp fixtures and their eight G-code goldens move from the
Linear lead to the Perpendicular lead; the dive point in each golden
moves from one radius off the part to the radius plus the lead. The
compensated ring itself did not move.

Fixes #3891

Co-Authored-By: GLM-5.3 <noreply@anthropic.com>
